[TEXT] The dmesg log tells the complete story. After startup, switch0's bridge converged normally (ports reached **forwarding** state), but then:

```
[164466.650757] br0: port 2(eth1) entered disabled state
[164466.650774] br0: port 1(eth0) entered disabled state
```

Both ports were disabled **simultaneously** (17 µs apart) — a clear signature of `ip link set br0 down` being run after the initial STP convergence. The bridge has received only 2 RX packets total since; no frames are being forwarded at all.

This is fully consistent with the symptom: IT hosts get **"Destination Host Unreachable"** (ARP to 192.168.1.1 fails) while CS hosts (through switch1, whose `br0` is UP and forwarding) are unaffected.

